{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA linked worktree's editable install records the project version in its `.dist-info`\nat install time. Rebasing that worktree onto a `main` that bumped the version does\n**not** refresh it, so `importlib.metadata.version(\"nava-rebar\")` keeps returning the\nold value while `pyproject.toml` says the new one.\n\nNothing warns. The mismatch surfaces only as a public-API-surface drift failure\nroughly 40 minutes into `make verify`, whose message names the baseline and tells\nyou to regenerate it — the opposite of the correct action. Following that advice\nwould commit a corrupted `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json`.\n\nThis cost one full 42-minute `make verify` run on story `19ba-bd62-1adb-41df` on\n2026-10-30, and the same trap was caught pre-emptively on `a018-a2c0-fc15-434c`\nminutes later, so it is not a one-off.\n\n## Observation (measured)\n\nIn `.rebar/worktrees/impl-19ba` after rebasing onto a `main` carrying 0.13.1 -> 0.14.0:\n\n- `pyproject.toml` declared `version = \"0.14.0\"`.\n- `.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nava_rebar-0.13.1.dist-info` was still present,\n  and `python -c 'import rebar; print(rebar.__version__)'` printed `0.13.1`.\n- `src/rebar/__init__.py:144` sets `__version__ = importlib.metadata.version(\"nava-rebar\")`,\n  so the stale dist-info is read straight into the public surface.\n- `make verify` failed with, verbatim:\n\n      Public API surface drift detected against the committed baseline\n      (tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json):\n        ~ CHANGED  rebar.__version__\n      If this change is intentional, refresh the baseline and review the diff:\n          python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update\n\n  from `tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py:78` and `:83`\n  (`test_committed_baseline_matches_live_surface`, `test_default_invocation_runs_the_check`).\n- Two further failures in the same run cleared on the rerun and are **not** attributed\n  here: `test_pytest_interleaved_conftest_args.py::test_conftest_fixtures_survive_a_parent_dir_file_arg_between_package_args`\n  and `test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py::test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone`.\n  Their failure output does not name a version, so their cause is unestablished.\n- `make install` in the worktree replaced the dist-info with `nava_rebar-0.14.0` and the\n  rerun was clean: 20,087 passed, 28 skipped, 0 failures.\n\nThe distribution name is `nava-rebar`, not `rebar`; a probe written as\n`importlib.metadata.version(\"rebar\")` raises `PackageNotFoundError` in every worktree\nand silently proves nothing. That misnaming is itself an easy way to miss this.\n\n### Independent reproduction (2026-10-31, before implementation)\n\nA throwaway worktree at `c9159d2af47^` (0.13.1), provisioned with `make venv` + the\n`uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra metrics` that `make install` runs, then given a\nlocal commit and `git rebase c9159d2af47` (the 0.14.0 bump):\n\n- `pyproject.toml` read `0.14.0`; site-packages held only `nava_rebar-0.13.1.dist-info`;\n  `rebar.__version__` was `0.13.1` while `rebar.__file__` was the worktree's own\n  `src/rebar/__init__.py`. The editable `.pth` keeps the *code* current; only the\n  install-time metadata is frozen. That is the root cause: the dist-info is written once\n  by the build backend at install time and nothing re-runs it on a checkout change.\n- `tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py` failed with the same `--update` advice.\n- `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update` in that env rewrote the baseline's\n  `__version__` from `'0.14.0'` to `'0.13.1'` — the corruption, confirmed by `git diff`.\n- The same trap sits in the documented release procedure: `docs/releasing.md` step 1\n  (lines ~313-321) bumps `pyproject.toml`, runs `uv lock`, then runs\n  `gen_api_surface.py --update` with no reinstall in between, so a releaser whose venv\n  predates the bump writes the OLD version into the baseline.\n- Re-running `uv sync --locked ...` replaced the dist-info with `nava_rebar-0.14.0` and\n  `rebar.__version__` printed `0.14.0`.\n- A directory holding a fake `nava_rebar-0.0.1.dist-info/METADATA`, put on `PYTHONPATH`,\n  shadows the real dist-info (`rebar.__version__` -> `0.0.1`, code still from `src/`).\n  This gives a hermetic, install-free way to reproduce the mismatch in a test.\n\n## Approach\n\nFollow the repo's existing pattern for an environment precondition that would otherwise\nfail late and misleadingly: `tests/conftest.py:173` `pytest_configure` calls\n`_git_floor.floor_violation()` (`tests/_git_floor.py`) and raises `pytest.UsageError`\nwith an actionable diagnostic, and `tests/conftest.py` `_select_repo_pandoc` already\nloads a `scripts/` module by path with `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location`.\n\n1. **One detector, in the gate script.** Add\n   `installed_version_drift(*, installed=None, declared=None) -> str | None` to\n   `scripts/gen_api_surface.py` (stdlib only, so the script stays standalone). It reads\n   the declared version from `pyproject.toml` `[project].version` with `tomllib` and the\n   installed one with `importlib.metadata.version(\"nava-rebar\")`. It returns `None` when\n   they are equal, when the distribution is not installed (`PackageNotFoundError`,\n   matching `src/rebar/__init__.py:146`'s source-tree fallback), or when `pyproject.toml`\n   carries no static version. Otherwise it returns a diagnostic naming both versions,\n   naming `make install` as the remedy, and saying not to regenerate the baseline. The\n   keyword overrides mirror `floor_violation(installed=..., floor=...)` for unit tests.\n2. **Fail the pytest session up front.** In `tests/conftest.py` `pytest_configure`,\n   next to the git-floor check, load `scripts/gen_api_surface.py` by path and raise\n   `pytest.UsageError(diagnostic)` when the detector returns one. This runs before\n   collection, so it precedes the surface gate and every other test in `make test`,\n   `make verify`, and bare `pytest`. An aligned environment (all of CI, which installs\n   fresh with `uv sync --locked`) gets `None` and no behaviour change.\n3. **Correct the gate's own advice.** In `gen_api_surface._check()` (lines 230-248):\n   when the detector reports a mismatch, write its diagnostic; and when the only drift\n   line is `~ CHANGED  rebar.__version__`, omit the `--update` recommendation. Drift in\n   other symbols keeps the existing `--update` text after the mismatch diagnostic.\n4. **Refuse to write the corruption.** `main([\"--update\"])` (lines 262-264) exits 2 with\n   the diagnostic and leaves the baseline untouched when the detector reports a\n   mismatch. This closes the release-procedure path above, which has no pytest session\n   in front of it.\n5. **Docs.** `AGENTS.md`: one sentence in the worktree bullet of the Git-workflow\n   section — run `make install` after any rebase that crosses a version bump.\n   `docs/releasing.md` step 1: run `make install` after `uv lock` and before\n   `gen_api_surface.py --update`, with one line saying why.\n\nRejected: a Makefile-only preflight (misses bare `pytest`); auto-reinstalling from\nconftest (mutates the venv from a test run); dropping `__version__` from the baseline\n(removes intended release-bump coverage and is a separate policy change).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `scripts/gen_api_surface.py` — detector, `_check()` message, `--update` refusal.\n- `tests/conftest.py` — `pytest_configure` precondition call.\n- `tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py` — new tests.\n- `AGENTS.md` — one sentence.\n- `docs/releasing.md` — reinstall step before `--update`.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew tests in `tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py`:\n\n- Detector unit cases: mismatch (`installed=\"0.13.1\"`, `declared=\"0.14.0\"`) returns text\n  containing both versions and `make install`; equal versions return `None`; a missing\n  distribution returns `None`.\n- End-to-end mismatch via the fake-dist-info `PYTHONPATH` shadow (tmp dir, no venv\n  mutation):\n  - `python -m pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py` exits with\n    pytest's usage-error code 4 and its output names both versions and `make install`\n    (AC1: the session stops before any test, including the surface gate, runs).\n  - `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check` exits 1, its stderr names `make install`\n    and does **not** contain `gen_api_surface.py --update` (AC3).\n  - `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update` with `BASELINE_PATH` untouched: exits 2\n    and the committed baseline bytes are unchanged (run against the real file, compared\n    by content before/after).\n- Aligned case (AC2): the existing `test_committed_baseline_matches_live_surface` and\n  `test_default_invocation_runs_the_check` stay green, and `installed_version_drift()`\n  with no overrides returns `None` in the test environment.\n- Red-before-fix: run the new tests against the unmodified script/conftest and record the\n  failures on this ticket.\n\nRun: `pytest tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py`, plus `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: In a worktree whose installed `nava-rebar` dist-info version differs from the\n      `version` in `pyproject.toml`, the mismatch is reported with a message naming both\n      versions and `make install` as the remedy, before the public-API surface gate runs.\n      Verified by the PYTHONPATH-shadow test: `pytest --collect-only` exits 4 with that text.\n- [ ] AC2: When the installed version matches `pyproject.toml`, no such message is\n      emitted and no existing behaviour changes. Verified by the existing surface-gate\n      tests passing and the detector returning `None` in the test environment.\n- [ ] AC3: When the only public-API surface drift is `rebar.__version__` and the installed\n      version disagrees with `pyproject.toml`, the surface-gate failure text does **not**\n      recommend `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update`. Verified by the\n      PYTHONPATH-shadow `--check` test.\n- [ ] AC4: `AGENTS.md` states that `make install` must be run after a rebase that crosses\n      a version bump; verified by `grep -n \"crosses a version bump\" AGENTS.md`.\n- [ ] AC5: New tests cover AC1, AC2 and AC3 and are red before the fix (failures recorded\n      as a ticket comment).\n- [ ] AC6: With a mismatched install, `gen_api_surface.py --update` exits 2 and leaves\n      `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` byte-identical; `docs/releasing.md` step 1\n      runs `make install` before `--update`. Verified by test and grep.\n- [ ] AC7: `pytest tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py`, `make lint` and `make typecheck`\n      pass locally, and the Gerrit change carries `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`\n      (Verified runs CI's full gating suite)."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793478579832738001,"uuid":"5601fd34-b300-4503-bf4b-97491083d4e6"}